				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1113,
				32
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add Workbench* Effect-TS service layers\n\nAdd six new workbench-tier service layers that bridge VS Code's native workbench services:\n- WorkbenchCommandService: Execute/list/filter commands, stream command execution events\n- WorkbenchDialogService: Confirm dialogs, pick choices, show info/warn/error\n- WorkbenchLifecycleService: Phase tracking (Starting/Ready/Restored/Eventually), shutdown streams\n- WorkbenchNotificationService: Dispatch notifications, stream dispatched events\n- WorkbenchStorageService: Scope-aware (Application/Profile/Workspace) storage with targets\n- WorkbenchThemeService: Get/set color themes, token color queries, theme change streams\n\nEach service provides a typed Effect-TS interface consumable via Effect.gen, with a Live implementation (runtime bridge via globalThis.__CEL_SERVICES__) and a Problem ADT for error cases. Services follow the established pattern in Wind of exposing Context.Tag, interface, and Layer for dependency injection.\n\nRefs: Land/.claude/tauri/Patches/14-StreamingGRPC.md",
			"SHA": "f41f7c778f681e7274ebec65953544dd251fd949"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T04:54:06Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1056,
				11
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add UserSettings and WorkbenchStorage Effect-TS services\n\nAdd two new workbench-tier services that bridge VS Code's native IConfigurationService and IStorageService:\n\n- UserSettingsService: Reads/writes user configuration via globalThis.__CEL_SERVICES__.Configuration and __CEL_OVERRIDE_CONFIG__. Supports Memory target for synchronous override writes and dispatches cel:user-settings-changed events. The Write path delegates to VS Code's updateValue for non-Memory targets.\n\n- WorkbenchStorageService: Scope-aware (Application/Profile/Workspace) storage bridge via globalThis.__CEL_SERVICES__.Storage. Provides Get/GetBoolean/GetNumber/GetObject/Store/Remove/Keys operations and a Changes stream for key mutations.\n\nBoth include Live implementations (runtime bridge to workbench) and Stub implementations (in-memory for tests/early boot). Each service exposes a Context.Tag, typed problem ADT, and interface for Effect.gen consumers.",
			"SHA": "b0f1a825237b399e7123d5026c8c86ec866acc32"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T03:48:33Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠁⠀⠀⠀",
				1035,
				223
			],
			"Message": "build(Wind): Minify ESBuild configuration and Target output files\n\nRebuild the ESBuild configuration files (BaseConfig, CompileConfig, TargetConfig, constants, and index files) and the compiled Target output with minification enabled. The Configuration/ESBuild source files are compressed from multi-line readable format to single-line minified output, while the Target/ directory files are rebuilt with reduced file sizes through variable renaming, dead code elimination, and compression.\n\nThis minification reduces the overall bundle size and improves load times for the Wind UI service layer.",
			"SHA": "7f0bfd4247712edcfac7b2780fac1424b85fa4ce"
		},
